@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
!include _uml-style.puml
title From settlement to exit status — UML state machine
hide empty description
hide stereotype

state "Settling cancellation" as Cancellation
state "Settling the original outcome" as Original
state "Settling required cleanup" as Cleanup
state "Writing the result" as Writing
state "Cancelled\n129: HUP\n130: INT\n143: TERM" as Cancelled <<outcome>>
state "Original failure retained\n1: no result\n2: invalid inputs or settings\n3: policy refusal or admission refusal\n5: worker, supervision or result failure\n124: selection deadline\n126: pre-start execution failure\n127: program or interpreter not found" as Failure <<outcome>>
state "5: cleanup, recovery or group failure" as CleanupFailure <<outcome>>
state "5: result write or flush failed" as WriteFailure <<outcome>>
state "0: exact result delivered" as Success <<outcome>>

[*] --> Cancellation
Cancellation -right-> Cancelled : [cancellation selected]
Cancellation --> Original : [no cancellation]
Original -right-> Failure : [original failure]
Original --> Cleanup : [valid candidate result]
Cleanup -right-> CleanupFailure : [required cleanup failed\nor group survives]
Cleanup -[#135E50]-> Writing : [reap, group absence and\nrequired cleanup confirmed]
Writing -right-> WriteFailure : write or flush fails
Writing -[#135E50]-> Success : write and flush succeed

legend bottom
  Refinement of chapter 3's settlement phase for start-session.
  Dot: entry to this detail. Blue boxes: conceptual settlement phases.
  Grey boxes: outcomes. Arrows: transitions. Brackets: conditions.
  Applicable cleanup is attempted before reporting an outcome.
  This order expresses precedence, not the implementation's call order.
  Original failures keep their status when later cleanup also fails.
  Cancellation suppresses a published result and retains other diagnostics.
  Green: the only success route. Empty publication is a valid value.
  A later nonzero child exit does not invalidate that value.
  A failed final write can leave a prefix; a late signal can interrupt it.
  end-session, help and version invocations are covered by the table, not this view.
endlegend
@enduml
